In `Rescaling.call`, the reshape block runs only when both parts of the condition are true: `len(scale_shape) > 0` and `backend.image_data_format() == "channels_first"`. The test explicitly sets the global image data format to `"channels_first"` and constructs `Rescaling` with `scale` as a NumPy vector `[0.5, 1.0, 1.5]`, so after casting, `scale_shape` is non-scalar and has positive length. That makes the condition true, so the branch containing the scale reshape is executed.

